# Golden image / 2026-27

Current lifecycle is config-driven through `config.toml` and `scripts/mct-vm.py`.

Before a new classroom image round:

1. Review `config.toml`, especially `[workflow]`, `[golden_image]` and `[run]`.
2. Review/update `rollout.csv` and run `./scripts/mct-vm.py generate-nix` if the
   active VM/student mapping changed.
3. Build the generic QCOW2 (`nix build .#qcow2`) and place/name it as configured.
4. Run `./scripts/mct-vm.py prepare-golden`.
5. Do the deliberate manual GUI work (VS Code extensions, Continue install/start,
   tests). `prepare-golden` has already installed the final reviewed Continue
   config, so test Continue with the same configuration students will receive.
6. Shut the golden VM down cleanly.
7. Run `./scripts/mct-vm.py finalize-golden`; this verifies the Continue config,
   removes Bash/Chrome manual-work traces without deleting Chrome preferences,
   installs the managed start page, and cleanly freezes the golden image.
8. Run `clone`, then `individualize` (pilot with `[run].only_vms` first).
9. Run `prepare-images`, `update-csv`, then `rollout`.

Lockdown and classroom are alternative workflow modes. Lockdown has different
seat assignments and is intentionally not being expanded/reworked right now.
